/-!
# VIII08 — the rotation `v` produced by the odd magnetic potential

`beta(t) = b_s(1/t)` (with `beta 0 = 0`) and

  `v(R) = ∫₀^{1/R} t (2j + 6 beta(t) - t r(t)) dt`.

Then, from the FTC and `beta(1/R) = b_s(R)`,

  `v'(R) = -(1/R³) (2j + 6 b_s(R) - r(1/R)/R)`,

so the angular-momentum defect is the ACTUAL source, not a definitional rewriting:

  `Dell[j, b_s, v](R) = R³ v'(R) + 6 b_s(R) + 2j = r(1/R)/R`  for all `R > 3`.

The bounds follow from `|beta(t)| ≤ B t/8` and `|r| ≤ Ar` on `K`:

  `R³ (v - j/R²) = R³ ∫₀^{1/R} (6 t beta(t) - t² r(t)) dt`,
  `|R³(v - j/R²)| ≤ B/4 + Ar/3`;
  `R⁴(v' + 2j/R³) = r(1/R) - 6 R b_s(R)`, `|R⁴(v' + 2j/R³)| ≤ 3B/4 + Ar`.
-/

